            <ArticleTitle>Trigeminal neuralgia: how to rule out the wrong treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>63-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Toothache is difficult to diagnose and treat appropriately when traditional dental diagnostic test results are negative. This study looked at 61 patients who were treated for pretrigeminal or trigeminal neuralgia. Of these, 61 percent were incorrectly diagnosed and treated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
